<http://data.silknow.org/object/7fa6e13d-ed49-31ac-897a-4aa6ddd4b580>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Piece, irregular shape, vaguely oval, with four semi-circles cut out at edges (probably a chair seat). Red woodblock (?) print on white ground pattern shows two pictorial oval medallions alternating horizontally and vertically.  In one, a milkmaid at a churn before a farm; in the other, chickens in farmyard. Interspaces dilled with sprays of carnations or daisies. A faded spot and a stain; several small holes."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/fb04d5b8-4676-34dd-8c5e-54d3da82bfdf> ;
